IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-prohibitions`

-- Competition Act 2004, ss 33, 34, 47, 54, 69, 71, 75, 77, 86 and Third and Fourth Schedules -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_competition-act-2004.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a price-fixing cartel` MEANS Agreement WITH
    `has an anti-competitive object or effect in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `would obstruct a service of general economic interest` IS FALSE
    `is made to comply with a legal requirement` IS FALSE
    `is excluded by a Ministerial order` IS FALSE
    `falls under another regulator's competition law` IS FALSE
    `relates to a specified activity` IS FALSE
    `relates to the Automated Clearing House` IS FALSE
    `is a vertical agreement` IS FALSE
    `is a vertical agreement specified by Ministerial order` IS FALSE
    `improves production or distribution or promotes progress` IS FALSE
    `imposes restrictions that are not indispensable` IS FALSE
    `could eliminate competition in a substantial part` IS FALSE
    `is directly related and necessary to a merger` IS FALSE
    `results in a merger` IS FALSE

